{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792933636,"nonce":"bDvtRfN9h8HjWRZ3tg8WP9IqwvY=","title":"Final red team, AFK run 20261024-1951, finding F1 (+ fix3-engine UNTOUCHED note). MED. Pre-existing.","message":"`executor.launch` can return Err after the Pod exists (k8s create accepted, then `ensure_step_secrets` fails, or the create response is lost; executor-k8s lib.rs ~2595). After a cancel, the redelivered launch is refused as no longer wanted (scheduler.rs ~3183 / ~3350) and marked dispatched without any teardown, so the CANCEL_ATTEMPT retires as \"gone\". The deterministically named Pod is never deleted and the target's hold ends while it runs. Same class: a replica crash after `executor.launch` but before `set_attempt_handle` — the redelivered launch is refused and that Pod is orphaned.\n\nFix: on the refusal branch, cancel the deterministic handle (delete-by-name, 404 = Ok) before dispatching.\nRepro (ignored): redteam_open_bugs_final.rs `a_unit_created_by_a_failed_launch_is_torn_down_after_a_cancel`.","files":null}]}